     Busy waiting :


   The

    goto L1

   (for readers) and

    goto L2

   (for writers) implement busy waiting by repeatedly checking conditions until access is granted.


    Yes, the above solution can lead to starvation of writers, as readers are given priority over writers.


    Reader


    In the solution, if a writer is waiting and a new reader arrives (

     W == 0

    ), the reader can proceed by incrementing

     R

    and entering the critical section.


    This means writers must wait until all readers finish reading, and if readers keep arriving, the writer is perpetually delayed.


    Readers only wait when a writer is actively writing. Once the writer is done, readers can proceed, so they don't experience starvation.


